{
	title: 'Automatic compaction before the window fills',
	spec: 'Before each provider round the host compares the context used by the last round (task 1g\'s context: input + cache read + cache write) with the model\'s context window; at or above the `compactAt` setting (config.ason, settings table, a fraction, default 0.85; 0 turns it off) it writes a compact record (task bc) first and tells the user with a notice in the transcript. Mid-turn this is safe because the boundary never splits a tool call from its result: the compact record goes only between rounds, after results are recorded. When a provider refuses a request because the prompt is too long (Anthropic "prompt is too long", OpenAI context_length_exceeded, and a 400/413 whose message says so) that is not a temporary failure to retry forever (item 80): the host compacts once and retries the round; if the compacted request is still too long, the turn fails with the provider\'s message. Tests with fake providers: the threshold triggers a compact between rounds, never between a call and its result; compactAt 0 never compacts; a too-long error compacts and retries once, then fails.',
	status: 'planned',
	needs: ['bc']
}
